<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet xml:id="G2_PP" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Graphing #2</title>

    <objectives>
                    <ul>
                <li>    <p>
                    <alert>G #2:</alert> I can sketch qualitative graphs given a written situation.     
                </p></li>
                    </ul>
            
    </objectives>

    <exercise>
        <p>
            A football is thrown into the air and allowed to fall to the ground, where it bounces once.  Draw a graph of the height of the ball in terms of the time since it was thrown.  
        </p>
        <image source="BlankGrid10.png" width="50%">
            <shortdescription>A blank grid for drawing</shortdescription>
        </image>
        <solution>
            <p>
              The ball should start at some positive height along the vertical axis indicating where it was thrown from.  
              The ball will gain altitude for a short amount of time and then fall back to the ground, this is shown by an
              increasing graph, followed by a decreasing segment that approaches the horizontal axis.  When the ball hits the 
              ground it bounces back up for a short amount of time and then again falls to the ground, represented by an
              additional increasing curve and a decreasing curve.
            </p>
            <image source="MTfootball.png" width="50%">
                <shortdescription>A qualitative graph representing the height of the football over time.</shortdescription>
            </image>
        </solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
        <p>
            A person enters an elevator on the ground floor and rides it up to the third floor of a building.  They walk around the corridor on that floor and then take an escalator back down to the ground level.  Draw a graph of the height of the person above ground in terms of the time since they first entered the elevator.  
        </p>
        <image source="BlankGrid10.png" width="50%">
            <shortdescription>Blank Grid for graphing</shortdescription>
        </image>
        <solution>
            <p>
                We start the graph at the origin with an increasing segment for a short length of time.  
                The straight line shows that the elevator is 
                going up at a constant rate. We then have a horizontal line indicating that they were at the same height 
                when they were walking around the third floor. A decreasing line segment shows they returned to the ground
                floor at a constant rate. 
            </p>
            <image source="MTelevator.png">
                <shortdescription>A qualitative graph as described in the solution.</shortdescription>
            </image>
        </solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
        <p>
            A vase is being filled with water at a constant rate, draw a qualitative graph that shows the height of the 
            water at a given time. 
        </p>
        <sidebyside>
        <image source="MTvase.png" width="40%">
            <shortdescription>Image of a vase with the width varying with height.</shortdescription>
        </image>
        <image source="BlankGrid10.png">
            <shortdescription>Blank grid for drawing</shortdescription>
        </image>
        </sidebyside>
        <solution>
            <p>
                The graph will be increasing the fastest when the height is increasing fastest.  This will occur when
                the the vase is the narrowest.
            </p>
            <image source="MTvaseS">
                <shortdescription>A graphical representation of height of the water</shortdescription>
            </image>
        </solution>
    </exercise>

</worksheet>